    "result_text": "All 286 tests pass, including the new `Cp17Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` rule for owner creation. When a new owner is created, the field is set to `true` if another owner already has the same address and city (compared ignoring case and whitespace), otherwise `false` \u2014 and creation is always allowed.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 In `saveOwner`, added `owner.setSharesHousehold(sharesHousehold(owner))` for new owners, and a `sharesHousehold(...)` helper that checks existing owners for a matching normalized address + city, reusing the existing `normalize` helper for consistency with the other rules.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `shares_household` mapped column with getter/setter (matching the `namesakeCount` style), so MapStruct auto-maps it into the response DTO.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n- **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `shares_household` column to the `owners` table (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none` with the hsqldb schema).\n\nThe value is computed at registration, persisted, and surfaced both on the create response and on `GET /api/owners/{id}` (which is what the acceptance test reads).",
